  "question": {
    "text": "The following statements relate to the adsorption of gases on a solid surface. Identify the <strong>incorrect</strong> statement among them:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Entropy of adsorption is negative",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Enthalpy of adsorption is negative",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "On adsorption decrease in surface energy appears as heat",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "On adsorption, the residual forces on the surface are increased",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Adsorption is spontaneous process <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> is -ve. During adsorption randomness of adsorbate molecules reduced and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>total</mi></msub></math> is +ve.<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is highly -ve and residual forces on surface are decreased.<br />&nbsp;"
  }
